or_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.8.dev7.official\n- Not tested in other versions\n- N/A in commits before #113429 was merged\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev7 - Bluefin 44.20261006 (Silverblue) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor (2560x1440 @ 144.00 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (nvidia; 615.71.09) - AMD Ryzen 5 9600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 30.45 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nCreate a Decal that uses a `StreamedTexture2D` and you'll see that it never loads lower LODs. As a workaround, I can override the maximum LOD to 0 for decal textures to force the lower LODs to load.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen the MRP and see that the decal texture is super blurry, even though the minimum LOD is set to 0.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[texture_streaming_decal_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33116860/texture_streaming_decal_mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124229/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}